PostgreSQL/Supabase migrations
==============================

When CURRENT_DATABASE=postgresql (or DATABASE_URL uses a PostgreSQL scheme),
Flask-Migrate uses this directory. The existing migrations/ directory remains
the MySQL migration history.

For a new, empty Supabase database, apply the baseline with:

    flask --app run db upgrade

Create later PostgreSQL migrations with:

    flask --app run db migrate -m "description"

Do not run the PostgreSQL baseline against a database containing application
tables. Check the Supabase Tables page first; this project does not inspect or
clear the remote database automatically.
